sts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T17:08:06Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T17:08:06Z","body":"I created an issue here: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103918\r\n\r\nI actually found that godot hangs when attempting to import a project.  I'm going to debug that.  I expect LLVM 19.1.7 has done us a favor and made it easy to reproduce some race conditions.  Hopefully it will fix this issue as well: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99128","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711275607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711397877","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103913#issuecomment-2711397877","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103913","id":2711397877,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hnKX1","user":{"login":"darksylinc","id":3395130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzOTUxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T17:56:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T17:56:37Z","body":"Hi!\r\n\r\nCould you post where the condition variable was waiting? (that could be on several other threads).\r\n\r\nI can't make sense of this bug because I see that `cond_var.wait(lock)` is only called in two places: _thread_function & _wait_collaboratively.\r\n\r\n`_thread_function` appears to call its own CV.\r\nIf I'm reading this correctly `_wait_collaboratively` is also calling its own CV because p_caller_pool_thread is its own:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid WorkerThreadPool::yield() {\r\n\tint th_index = get_thread_index();\r\n\tERR_FAIL_COND_MSG(th_index == -1, \"This function can only be called from a worker thread.\");\r\n\t_wait_collaboratively(&threads[th_index], ThreadData::YIELDING);\r\n...\r\n}\r\n\r\nError WorkerThreadPool::wait_for_task_completion(TaskID p_task_id) {\r\n...\r\n\tThreadData *caller_pool_thread = thread_ids.has(Thread::get_caller_id()) ? &threads[thread_ids[Thread::get_caller_id()]] : nullptr;\r\n...\r\n\t_wait_collaboratively(caller_pool_thread, task);\r\n....\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis means that, unless I'm seeing this wrong, only one thread ever waits on its own CV. Therefore notify_one() and notify_all() should behave exactly the same.\r\n\r\nnotify_all() makes sense when more than one thread are waiting on the same CV. I wish to understand better how is this happening and the potential race conditions that can arise from such thing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711397877/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711408815","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103913#issuecomment-2711408815","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103913","id":2711408815,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hnNCv","user":{"login":"TCROC","id":24307049,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzA3MDQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24307049?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC","html_url":"https://github.com/TCROC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-10T18:01:10Z","updated_at":"2025-03-10T18:01:10Z","body":"Yep.  I'll go do that.  Also, are you in the godot dev chat?  If you want, we can hop in a call over there and I can share my screen / step through the debugger.\r\n\r\nhttps://chat.godotengine.org/channel/devel?msg=owsrr2DTFiF2E3c9J","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2711408815/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,